[B]Keep VPNs, proxies, Tor and bot hosts off your server.[/B] VPNDetection checks each player's address as they join, and refuses or flags to your staff the ones who come through a VPN, a proxy, Tor or a hosting network.

[SIZE=5][B]🎯 What it stops[/B][/SIZE]
[LIST]
[*]Banned players coming back on a new address
[*]Bots flooding in from rented servers
[*]Players from countries you don't want, or from any but the ones you list
[/LIST]

[SIZE=5][B]⚡ Up in a minute[/B][/SIZE]
[LIST=1]
[*]Put the jar in your server's plugins folder and restart
[*]VPNs, Tor and hosting networks are blocked from the first join, with no account
[*]On a network, install it on the proxy alone: Velocity or BungeeCord sees each player once ([URL=https://github.com/vpndetection-io/minecraft-plugin#getting-started]the README[/URL] has both)
[/LIST]

[SIZE=5][B]🔧 You decide what happens[/B][/SIZE]
[LIST]
[*]Block, alert your staff or allow, separately for VPNs, Tor, hosting networks, proxies and privacy relays
[*]Rules on any field of the answer, like one VPN provider or one network
[*]Your own kick and alert messages, with color codes
[*]A bypass list for players, addresses and ranges
[*]/vpnd check looks up any player or address on the spot
[/LIST]

[SIZE=5][B]🎁 Free to start[/B][/SIZE]
[LIST]
[*]No account: VPNs, Tor, hosting networks, privacy relays and countries, on every join
[*]Free account, signed in with /vpnd login: every check, proxies included, for 100 lookups a day
[*]Paid plan: every check on every join, with the provider named in your messages
[/LIST]

[SIZE=5][B]🚀 Built for busy servers[/B][/SIZE]
[LIST]
[*]One jar for Paper, Spigot, Purpur, Folia, Velocity and BungeeCord, on Java 17 or newer
[*]A login waits at most 2.5 seconds, and on a proxy the lookup runs while the player signs in
[*]If our API can't be reached, players are let in, unless you set it to refuse them
[*]Each answer is kept for an hour, so a player who rejoins costs no second lookup
[/LIST]

[SIZE=5][B]🔒 What it sends[/B][/SIZE]
For each player who joins, the plugin sends their address to api.vpndetection.io and nothing else about them: no name, no UUID. Requests name the plugin, its version and your server software. [URL=https://vpndetection.io/privacy]Privacy policy[/URL]

[SIZE=5][B]💬 Setup and help[/B][/SIZE]
Every setting, command and rule: [URL=https://docs.vpndetection.io/integrations/minecraft]docs.vpndetection.io/integrations/minecraft[/URL]. The source: [URL=https://github.com/vpndetection-io/minecraft-plugin]GitHub[/URL]. Questions: support@vpndetection.io
